"'''Sweet Melody'''" is a song by British girl group [[Little Mix]], released through [[RCA Records]] on 23 October 2020, as the third single from the group's sixth studio album ''[[Confetti (Little Mix album)|Confetti]]'' (2020). Little Mix worked with notable names and frequent collaborators [[Tayla Parx]], [[Morten Ristorp]], Robin Frid, Brian Garcia, and [[MNEK]], who co-written and co-produced the track. It has since been regarded as one of the group's best releases.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Stroude |first=Will |date=2021-11-11 |title=Little Mix's 32 singles ranked in order of greatness |url=https://www.attitude.co.uk/culture/film-tv/little-mixs-32-singles-ranked-in-order-of-greatness-304079/ |access-date=2023-06-10 |website=Attitude |language=en-GB}}</ref>

"Sweet Melody" was met with widespread acclaim from music critics who described it as a girl group classic<ref name=":1" /> with some citing it as a stand out single amongst their previous releases<ref>{{Cite web |date=2020-10-23 |title=Little Mix wow's with their new single and video Sweet Melody |url=https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/little-mix-wows-with-their-new-single-and-video-sweet-melody/ |access-date=2023-06-10 |website=GAY TIMES |language=en-GB}}</ref> and lead single material from the group's sixth album [[Confetti (Little Mix album)|''Confetti'']].<ref>{{Cite magazine |author=Billboard Staff |date=2020-12-11 |title=The 30 Best Pop Songs of 2020: Staff Picks |url=https://www.billboard.com/media/lists/best-pop-songs-2020-9497730/ |access-date=2023-06-10 |magazine=Billboard |language=en-US}}</ref> Furthermore, praise was given towards the song's production; describing it as "perfectly structured" with Billboard naming it as one of the best releases of 2020.<ref name=":2">{{Cite magazine |author=Billboard Staff |date=2020-12-08 |title=The 100 Best Songs of 2020: Staff List |url=https://www.billboard.com/media/lists/best-songs-2020-top-100-9494940/ |access-date=2022-03-25 |magazine=Billboard |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |author=Billboard Staff |date=2020-12-11 |title=The 30 Best Pop Songs of 2020: Staff Picks |url=https://www.billboard.com/media/lists/best-pop-songs-2020-9497730/ |access-date=2023-06-10 |magazine=Billboard |language=en-US}}</ref> It peaked at number one on the [[UK Singles Chart]], in January 2021, becoming the group's fifth number one single in the UK and their first since "[[Shout Out to My Ex]]" was released in 2016. It reached the top ten in five other territories.

An accompanying choreography-based music video was released and features individual and group shots of the members performing dance routines, filmed in an abandoned warehouse. It would mark the group's last music video with [[Jesy Nelson]], who left the group in the same year. The video was later nominated for "Best Pop Video" at the 2021 [[UK Music Video Awards]]. To promote the song, the group performed the track at the [[2020 MTV Europe Music Awards]], in which they co-hosted and performed it on [[The Jonathan Ross Show]], and [[Little Mix The Search]].

